//! protobus for Rust: RPC, server streaming and events between services, over
//! RabbitMQ, with Protocol Buffers as the contract.
//!
//! This is the Rust port of [protobus](https://github.com/ArielLaub/protobus)
//! (TypeScript). It speaks the same wire protocol as every other port, so
//! services and clients in any of them share one broker, one schema and even
//! one queue.
//!
//! - A [`Context`] is one process's place on the bus.
//! - A [`MessageService`] serves requests; code generated by `protobus-build`
//!   gives each proto service a typed handler trait.
//! - A [`ServiceProxy`] calls a service; generated proxies are typed.
//! - [`testing::MemoryBroker`] runs all of it in-process, without RabbitMQ.
//!
//! Everything here is `Send + Sync` and built for a multi-threaded tokio
//! runtime: handlers run in parallel on the runtime's workers, and no lock is
//! held across an await.

